## Defect found and fixed
The provisioned dashboard queried a Prometheus metric `ALWAYSON_STATIC{metric=...}`
from 10 stat panels. That metric does not exist and nothing in the tree writes it
(`grep -r ALWAYSON_STATIC` matched only the generator itself). All 10 stat panels
rendered "No data". Only the static nodeGraph and a text panel worked.

## Approach chosen
Grafana keeps PostgreSQL as its only datasource. Because the live health facts
(podman/systemd/sockets/disks/GPU) are not held in any database, a read-only host
collector projects them into PostgreSQL schema `ao_status`. Grafana's only panel
source is `SELECT` from that schema. No Prometheus datasource, no shell,
no container control — consistent with the §6.A.2 GUI boundary.

### SQLite
Grafana OSS 11.6.0 bundles no SQLite datasource, and the SQLite stores are host
paths the container cannot see. Rather than install an unsigned plugin and bind
mount personal databases into the container, the collector opens each declared
store read-only on the host (`file:...?mode=ro` + `PRAGMA query_only=ON`) and
projects counts/metadata into the same schema. Counts only — never message
bodies, mail, browsing history or credentials.

