## Starting state, measured 2026-10-02

- `ao-grafana.service` active, `127.0.0.1:3001`, `/api/health` → `database: ok`, 11.6.0
- Provisioning had exactly one datasource file: `datasources/prometheus.yml`,
  `url: http://ao-prometheus:9090`, `isDefault: true`
- `ao-grafana.container` carried `Requires=ao-prometheus.service`
- The 10 stat panels queried `ALWAYSON_STATIC{metric="..."}` against Prometheus.
  **`ALWAYSON_STATIC` does not exist** — `grep -r ALWAYSON_STATIC` matched only
  `generate-topology.py`, so all 10 tiles rendered "No data".

## Design: why a projection instead of a direct datasource

Live health facts (podman, systemd, sockets, disks, GPU) are not held in any
database, so with a PostgreSQL-only datasource something has to project them into
PostgreSQL. The same pattern covers SQLite without touching Grafana's boundary.

## Change

1. `config/platform/postgresql/ao-status.sql` — new. Schema `ao_status` in the
   existing `grafana` database: `fact_generated`, `container`, `container_network`,
   `network`, `unit`, `listener`, `disk`, `gpu`, `sqlite_store`, `sqlite_metric`,
   plus view `v_system_health`. Idempotent, no secret.
2. `scripts/operations/collect-system-health.py` — new. Read-only host inspection;
   writes the projection in one transaction. `--dry-run` needs no database.
3. `quadlet/operations/ao-status-collect.{service,timer}` — new. 60 s,
   `Persistent=true`, armed on `graphical-session.target`; password from the
   existing 0600 `reporting-grafana-postgres.env`.
4. Datasource swap. `datasources/prometheus.yml` **deleted**;
   `postgres-aostatus.yml` added over the already-mounted `/var/run/postgresql`
   socket — no new listener, no new network. `Requires=ao-prometheus.service`
   removed from `ao-grafana.container` and redeployed flat to
   `~/.config/containers/systemd/`. `ao-prometheus.*` was not opened, edited,
   stopped or restarted.
5. `scripts/operations/generate-topology.py` → `grafana_dashboard()` rewritten:
   30 panels / 6 rows. The JSON is generated, so the dead `ALWAYSON_STATIC`
   panels were fixed at source; a hand-edit would be overwritten on next run.
6. `README.md` — §19.2 items **89, 90, 91** added; §20 evidence row added.
   Item 87 (the original defect) was already closed.


## SQLite coverage

Grafana OSS 11.6.0 bundles 19 datasources and **none is SQLite** (verified in the
running container). Direct SQLite drill-down would need an unsigned third-party
plugin **plus** read-only bind mounts of personal databases (OpenClaw state, the
72M Akonadi db, browser profiles) — conflicting with §6.A.3 and §4.3.
**Rejected**; recorded as item 91.

Instead the five README §4.3 stores are opened **on the host**, read-only
(`file:...?mode=ro` + `PRAGMA query_only=ON`), and only **metadata and row counts**
are projected. No mount, no unsigned code, no personal data crossing the boundary.

Measured: **3 present** (OpenClaw 74 tables WAL, Akonadi 18 tables, Podman
metadata), **2 absent** — MeshChatX and QGroundControl do not exist on this host.
Recorded `present=false`; **no row invented**. Item 90.

